---
id: research-report
title: A sourced research report
purpose: An agent reads the knowledge base and the web, registers one sourced report, and an independent verifier checks it before a reviewer accepts.
use_when: The user asks a research question and wants findings that each cite a source.
produces: The registered report `root.report` (a reference, independently assessed), the text outputs `root.progress_note`, `root.summary` and `root.caveats`, then one review Human Task. Approving it accepts the mission.
slots:
  application_id:
    description: This server's application id (the start page names it).
    example: demo-app
  mission_key:
    description: "A stable slug for the mission: lower case letters, digits, `-` or `_`."
    example: research-report
  title:
    description: A one-line title.
    example: What published sources say about agent memory
  request:
    description: The user's request in their own words, verbatim, one line.
    example: Find out what is known about long-term memory for coding agents, with sources I can check.
  question:
    description: One question you asked in the interview. Add one `answers` entry for each further question.
    example: Which sources count as evidence, and how recent must they be?
  answer:
    description: The user's answer to that question, verbatim, one line.
    example: Published papers and vendor documentation from the last two years.
  done_means:
    description: What the user said finished looks like, verbatim, one line.
    example: A report where I can follow every finding to its source.
  out_of_scope:
    description: What the user ruled out, verbatim, one line. Delete the `out_of_scope` entry when they ruled out nothing.
    example: No benchmarks of our own.
  goal:
    description: The research question in the user's words, one line. Name the sources that count and how recent they must be.
    example: What do published sources from the last two years say about long-term memory for coding agents?
  criterion:
    description: How the reviewer knows it is done, one line.
    example: Every finding cites a source the report registers and the limits are stated.
  model_profile:
    description: The producer's Model Profile (topic `models`).
    example: producer.default
  verifier_model_profile:
    description: The verifier's Model Profile; prefer another vendor than the producer's.
    example: judge.default
  sandbox_profile:
    description: A sandbox profile bound on this installation (topic `manifest`).
    example: research.standard
  budget_usd:
    description: The ceiling on model spend in US dollars, a number.
    example: "2"
notes:
  - A Goal Loop of at most two iterations. The verifier's findings return to the executor as repair feedback.
  - The knowledge cognition plugin mounts the method skills by exact pin, `knowledge-research` (how to search, capture, cite and verify) and `knowledge-verify` (sources as evidence), with this application's knowledge charter (what counts as a source here) and the evidence capture server the method requires (capture a source as exact bytes, read it, locate a quote). The goal text carries the question only; each tool describes itself.
  - The code research plugin mounts Context7 for a first look at a library's documentation and GitHub, read-only, for the file at a release's commit.
  - A plugin on this lane is run as its members, so each member needs its own launch binding on the installation. The capture server also needs the installation's endpoint for it, and GitHub a read-only token; topic `capabilities` lists what each one needs.
  - The report is judged by the installation's trusted assessment. A start is refused with `trusted_assessment_unavailable` where none is composed.
  - The web research plugin needs its servers' secrets; preflight lists the ones that are missing.
  - The `brief` block is the interview's result in the user's words. The executor and the verifier are both told the purpose, the request, what done means, what each was given and each criterion whose `evidence` names an output.
---
manifest: mission/v2
mission:
  key: {{mission_key}}
  application: {{application_id}}
  title: >-
    {{title}}
  description: >-
    {{goal}}
  brief:
    purpose: research
    request: >-
      {{request}}
    answers:
      - question: >-
          {{question}}
        answer: >-
          {{answer}}
    done_means: >-
      {{done_means}}
    out_of_scope:
      - >-
        {{out_of_scope}}
  goals:
    - key: sourced_report
      description: >-
        {{goal}}
        Answer from the knowledge base and the web. Register one report whose every finding
        cites a source, and submit the named outputs.
      importance: primary
      objectives:
        - key: research_and_register
          description: Read the knowledge base and the web, register the sourced report and submit the named outputs.
      criteria:
        - key: report_assessed
          description: >-
            {{criterion}}
          evidence: [report, progress_note]
          acceptance:
            human: review_accept
  environment:
    lane: deep_agents
    model:
      profile: {{model_profile}}
    sandbox:
      profile: {{sandbox_profile}}
    plugins:
      - pin: plugin.web-research@latest
        as: web_research
      - pin: plugin.cognition-knowledge@latest
        as: knowledge_cognition
      - pin: plugin.code-research@latest
        as: code_research
    capabilities:
      - {pin: tool.knowledge-read-intent@latest, kind: tool, as: knowledge_search}
      - {pin: tool.knowledge-read@latest, kind: tool, as: knowledge_read}
      - {pin: tool.knowledge-report-register@latest, kind: tool, as: report_register}
      - {pin: tool.knowledge-submit-output@latest, kind: tool, as: submit_output}
    budget:
      usd: {{budget_usd}}
      tokens: 600000
      wall_clock: 45m
      tool_calls: 60
    governors:
      depth: 1
      fan_out: 2
      iterations: 2
      patience: 1
    side_effects: [read_only, workspace_write, external_write_reversible]
  program:
    key: root
    behavior: goal_loop
    objective: sourced_report
    action_space: [web_research, code_research, knowledge_cognition, knowledge_search, knowledge_read, report_register, submit_output]
    verifier:
      independent: true
      environment:
        model:
          profile: {{verifier_model_profile}}
    outputs:
      - name: report
        form: reference
        enforcement: required
        requirements:
          - {key: assessed, validator: "knowledge.report.assess@1"}
      - {name: progress_note, form: text, enforcement: required, media_type: text/plain, scope: iteration}
      - {name: summary, form: text, enforcement: expected, media_type: text/plain, scope: iteration}
      - {name: caveats, form: text, enforcement: optional, media_type: text/plain, scope: iteration}
  controls:
    commands_allowed: [pause, resume, cancel, queue_instruction, add_context]
